# ── Rust (optional extension build) ───────────────────────────────────────────
aegis_rust_v2/target/
**/target/
# Cargo.lock is currently git-ignored. Committing it (correct for a cdylib
# extension, and required to OSV/Trivy-scan the Rust tree) is blocked on a
# dependency-upgrade effort to clear pre-existing advisories in the pinned
# tree (pyo3 0.24→0.29: GHSA-36hh-v3qg-5jq4 / GHSA-chgr-c6px-7xpp; hickory-proto
# via reqwest: GHSA-3v94-mw7p-v465 [no fix yet] / GHSA-q2qq-hmj6-3wpp). Tracked
# in docs/ROADMAP.md. Until then cargo-audit (with documented ignores) covers Rust.
Cargo.lock

